& Sealed Types",           "course_name": "Object-Oriented Programming",           "unit_title": "Unit 2: Inheritance, Subtyping & Dynamic Polymorphism",           "difficulty": "Hard",           "duration_hours": 3,           "status": "pending",           "is_completed": false         },         {           "id": "task-top-203-4-3-2",           "topic_id": "top-203-4-3",           "date": "Day 2 (Sat, Nov 7)",           "day_number": 2,           "type": "study",           "title": "CS203: Byte and Character Streams, File I/O & Object Serialization",           "course_name": "Object-Oriented Programming",           "unit_title": "Unit 4: Exception Handling, Stream I/O & File Processing",           "difficulty": "Hard",           "duration_hours": 3,           "status": "pending",           "is_completed": false         },         {           "id": "task-top-203-5-1-3",           "topic_id": "top-203-5-1",           "date": "Day 3 (Sun, Nov 8)",           "day_number": 3,           "type": "study",           "title": "CS203: Generic Classes, Type Parameters & Invariance Guarantees",           "course_name": "Object-Oriented Programming",           "unit_title": "Unit 5: Generics, Collections Framework & Concurrency Basics",           "difficulty": "Hard",           "duration_hours": 3,           "status": "pending",           "is_completed": false         },         {           "id": "task-top-203-5-3-4",           "topic_id": "top-203-5-3",           "date": "Day 4 (Mon, Nov 9)",           "day_number": 4,           "type": "study",           "title": "CS203: Multi-threading Foundations: Thread Lifecycle & Synchronization Locks",           "course_name": "Object-Oriented Programming",           "unit_title": "Unit 5: Generics, Collections Framework & Concurrency Basics",           "difficulty": "Hard",           "duration_hours": 3,           "status": "pending",           "is_completed": false         },         {           "id": "task-mock-5-1793933494726",           "date": "Day 5 (Tue, Nov 10)",           "day_number": 5,           "type": "mock_test",           "title": "Comprehensive Diagnostic Mock Exam #1",           "course_name": "All Enrolled Courses",           "duration_hours": 3,           "status": "pending",           "is_completed": false         },         {           "id": "task-rev-6-1793933494726",           "date": "Day 6 (Wed, Nov 11)",           "day_number": 6,           "type": "revision",           "title": "Syllabus Consolidation & Formula Flashcards (CS201)",           "course_name": "Data Structures and Algorithms",           "duration_hours": 3,           "status": "pending",           "is_completed": false         },         {           "id": "task-buf-7-1793933494726",           "date": "Day 7 (Thu, Nov 12)",           "day_number": 7,           "type": "buffer",           "title": "Adaptive Buffer Day (Catch-up / Cognitive Rest & Consolidation)",           "course_name": "All Enrolled Courses",           "duration_hours": 2,           "status": "pending",           "is_completed": false         }       ]     }   },   "studentChatHistories": {     "student-1": {       "course-cs101:unit-101-2": [         {           "id": "msg-test-2-u",           "role": "user",           "content": "How do Python list comprehensions work?",           "timestamp": "10:05 AM"         },         {           "id": "msg-test-2-a",           "role": "assistant",           "content": "List comprehensions offer a concise syntax to create lists based on existing iterables.",           "timestamp": "10:06 AM"         }       ],       "course-cs201:unit-5": [         {           "id": "msg-test-dsa-u",           "role": "user",           "content": "Explain worst-case time complexity of quicksort.",           "timestamp": "10:15 AM"         }       ],       "course-cs201:all": [         {           "id": "msg-u-1793933787297-0iheg",           "role": "user",           "content": "Explain avl trees",           "timestamp": "08:26 am"         },         {           "id": "msg-a-1793933797395-7cvi2",           "role": "assistant",           "content": "Hello! As your EDUAGENT for CS201, I am happy to explain **AVL Trees**.\n\n### 1. Definition\nAn **AVL Tree** (named after inventors Adelson-Velsky and Landis) is a **self-balancing Binary Search Tree (BST)**. In a standard BST, the tree can become skewed (resembling a linked list) in the worst case, leading to $O(n)$ search time. An AVL tree maintains a height of $O(\\log n)$ by ensuring the tree remains balanced after every insertion and deletion.\n\n### 2. The Balance Factor (BF)\nThe core invariant of an AVL tree is the **Balance Factor**. For every node in the tree, the following condition must hold:\n$$\\text{Balance Factor (BF)} = \\text{Height(Left Subtree)} - \\text{Height(Right Subtree)}$$\n**Invariant:** $BF \\in \\{-1, 0, 1\\}$\n\nIf the BF of any node becomes $2$ or $-2$, the tree is considered unbalanced and requires a rotation.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Rotations\nWhen an insertion or deletion causes a node to have a BF of $\\pm 2$, we perform rotations to restore balance. There are four primary cases:\n\n#### A. Left-Left (LL) Case\n*   **Scenario:** A node becomes unbalanced due to an insertion in the left child's left subtree.\n*   **Fix:** Perform a **Single Right Rotation** on the unbalanced node.\n\n#### B. Right-Right (RR) Case\n*   **Scenario:** A node becomes unbalanced due to an insertion in the right child's right subtree.\n*   **Fix:** Perform a **Single Left Rotation** on the unbalanced node.\n\n#### C. Left-Right (LR) Case\n*   **Scenario:** Insertion in the left child's right subtree.\n*   **Fix:** Perform a **Left Rotation** on the left child, followed by a **Right Rotation** on the unbalanced node.\n\n#### D. Right-Left (RL) Case\n*   **Scenario:** Insertion in the right child's left subtree.\n*   **Fix:** Perform a **Right Rotation** on the right child, followed by a **Left Rotation** on the unbalanced node.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Complexity Analysis\nBecause the AVL tree maintains a height of $O(\\log n)$, all primary operations are highly efficient:\n\n| Operation | Time Complexity |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Search** | $O(\\log n)$ |\n| **Insertion** | $O(\\log n)$ |\n| **Deletion** | $O(\\log n)$ |\n\n*Note: While insertion/deletion is $O(\\log n)$, the constant factor is higher than a standard BST due to the overhead of calculating heights and performing rotations.*\n\n---\n\n### 5. Conceptual Diagram (LL Rotation Example)\nIf we have a tree where node `C` is unbalanced:\n\n**Before Rotation (LL Case):**\n```text\n      C (BF=2)\n     /\n    B (BF=1)\n   /\n  A\n```\n**After Right Rotation:**\n```text\n    B\n   / \\\n  A   C\n```\n\n### Study Tip for CS201:\nWhen practicing AVL trees, always remember to **update the height of the nodes** after a rotation. A common mistake in exams is forgetting that the height of a node is `1 + max(height(left), height(right))`.\n\nDo you have a specific insertion sequence you would like to walk through, or would you like to compare AVL trees with another self-balancing structure like Red-Black trees?",           "steps": [             {               "step": "Analysing Student Request",               "description": "Evaluating semantic intent: \"Explain avl trees\"",               "status": "completed"             },             {               "step": "Checking Academic Syllabus",               "description": "Verified alignment with CS201: Data Structures and Algorithms (All Units).",               "status": "completed"             },             {               "step": "Selecting Specialised Agent",               "description": "Routed request to Academic Tutor Agent.",               "status": "completed"             },             {               "step": "Executing Agentic Task",               "description": "Executing specialized workflow with 3-key rotation pool and grounded syllabus notes.",               "status": "completed"             },             {               "step": "Validating Results",               "description": "Verified academic integrity, formatting standards, and credential safety.",               "status": "completed"             },             {               "step": "Delivering Final Response",               "description": "Delivered synthesized educational guidance to student workspace.",               "status": "completed"             }           ],           "selectedAgent": "Academic Tutor Agent",           "timestamp": "08:26 am"         }       ]     }   } }